        "id": 1000094
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-26T05:49:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why was 440mA selected (there does not seem to be a related bug for this change).\nOur max is for DP alt mode which is 1.5W, so I could see an argument that 310mA is too low if the 5V supply is low. But wouldn\u0027t the 370mA cover that case and limit the worst case?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 328,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 328,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "4910259b0a264da7baa89ec5a1efbe22be9c1173",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ae920aee_bc17fe21",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/anx7447.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 328,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291180
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-26T06:15:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We have 4 level OCP threshold (240mA, 310mA, 370mA, 440mA) for VCONN, based on our experience, some kind of dongle takes more power(around ~2W). For 440mA select, just set for the maximum margin.",
      "parentUuid": "d483a7b5_e7be105a",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 328,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 328,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "4910259b0a264da7baa89ec5a1efbe22be9c1173",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "70da5b1e_5d966c8d",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/anx7447.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 328,
      "author": {
        "id": 1259838
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-27T15:51:11Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you add this information to the code (e.g. that some dongle take 2W of power so we increase the limit to 440mA)",
      "parentUuid": "ae920aee_bc17fe21",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 328,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 328,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "4910259b0a264da7baa89ec5a1efbe22be9c1173",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ead0277c_5630b7dd",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/anx7447.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 328,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000094
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-06-27T17:42:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You need to check with the board designer how much current they allocated for the Vconn. Change from 1.5W to 2W on two ports would mean the 5V supply needs to be designed to give 1W more. (Of course you get away with it most of the time because you are not loading down all the ports, but you still need to set this on a board (ref design) basis depending on the design parameter. Given the requirement is to match the AltMode spec it is reasonable boards were designed for 1.5W plus over-current margin)",
      "parentUuid": "70da5b1e_5d966c8d",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 328,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 328,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "4910259b0a264da7baa89ec5a1efbe22be9c1173",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "bcce807d_f3864a31",
        "filename": "driver/tcpm/anx7447.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 328,
      "author": {
        "id": 1291180
      },
      "writtenOn": "2018-07-03T03:26:48Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll change the VCONN current threshold to 370mA.",
      "parentUuid": "ead0277c_5630b7dd",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 328,
        "startChar": 56,
        "endLine": 328,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "4910259b0a264da7baa89ec5a1efbe22be9c1173",
